{"metadata":{"title":"value","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLElisionV5valueSSvp","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"value"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"}],"symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The value of this element."}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLElision"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlelision\/value"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLElision\/value"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"value","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLElision/value":{"title":"value","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The value of this element."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"value","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLElision\/value","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlelision\/value"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLElision":{"title":"MXLElision","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLElision","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The elision type represents an elision between lyric syllables. The text content specifies the symbol used to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"display the elision. Common values are a no-break space (Unicode 00A0), an underscore (Unicode 005F), or an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"undertie (Unicode 203F). If the text content is empty, the smufl attribute is used to specify the symbol to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"use. Its value is a SMuFL canonical glyph name that starts with lyrics. The SMuFL attribute is ignored if the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elision glyph is already specified by the text content. If neither text content nor a smufl attribute are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"present, the elision glyph is application-specific."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLElision"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLElision","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlelision"}}}